      paragraphs: [
        'How many halves are in 3 wholes? Six. That is what dividing by a fraction asks: how many of that fraction fit inside?\n[[3 ÷ 1/2 = 6]]',
        "The rule:\n[[To divide by a fraction, flip it and multiply.]]\nLet's look at an example:\n[[2/3 ÷ 1/6]]\nFirst, flip the second fraction: 1/6 becomes **6/1**.\nThen, multiply: 2/3 x 6/1 is **12/3**.\nThen, simplify: 12 divided by 3 is 4.\n[[2/3 ÷ 1/6 = 4]]",
        'Check with common sense. Dividing by something smaller than 1 makes the answer bigger, because more small pieces fit. Four sixths fit in two thirds, and 4 is bigger than 2/3.',
      ],
