        'A strong reason is something that is relevant and backed by something you can check. A weak reason is a feeling dressed up as a fact, or something that has nothing to do with the claim.',
        'When you read an argument, find the claim first. Then, ask:\n[[Does this support the claim, or is it just next to it?]]\n[[Claim = The Point]]\n[[Reason = The support for it]]',
