        'Look at three things:\nWhat the character **wants**.\nWhat the character **fears**.\nWhat the character does when **nobody is watching**.\nActions under pressure show motive more clearly than anything a character says.',
        'A good reading of a motive can point to the lines that support it. Without lines, it is a guess about the character, not a reading of the story.\n[[Motive = what a character wants or fears, shown by what they do]]',
