        "Let's look at two reports of the same event.\n[[The council voted 5 to 4 to raise the parking fee.]]\n[[The council rammed through a parking tax over furious objections.]]\nBoth are true. The first reports. The second leans, and the words doing the leaning are **rammed**, **tax** and **furious**.",
