        "Let's look at an example. 1,000 dollars at 10 percent a year, compounded yearly.\nAfter one year: 1,000 x 1.1 is **1,100**.\nAfter two years: 1,100 x 1.1 is **1,210**. That extra 10 is interest on last year's interest.\nAfter three years: 1,210 x 1.1 is **1,331**.\n[[1,000 x 1.1³ = 1,331]]",
        "The same rule runs a debt. A credit card balance compounds against you exactly as savings compound for you. Time is the whole trick: start early and the growth does most of the work.",
