        "Let's follow a bite of apple. Your teeth and stomach break it down: digestive. The useful parts pass into the blood: circulatory. Your cells burn them with oxygen the lungs brought in: respiratory. Your brain decided to take the bite in the first place: nervous. Your jaw muscles did the chewing: muscular. One bite, five systems.",
        "The systems depend on each other. Stop the lungs and the blood has no oxygen to carry. Stop the heart and the oxygen goes nowhere. When you name a system, ask what it does and which other systems it needs.",
        'Each system has a job. The nervous system senses and decides. The muscles move the body. The bones hold it up. The skull guards the brain. The stomach breaks down food.',
