        "Let's follow the parts. Water comes up from the roots. Carbon dioxide comes in through tiny holes in the leaf. Sunlight lands on the chloroplasts. The plant uses the light\'s energy to join the water and carbon dioxide into sugar, and oxygen is left over. The plant keeps the sugar and lets the oxygen out.",
